lto-disabled-list (81deepin1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial UOS package, populated from the UOS archive LTO rebuild
    on x86_64 (Shuttle batch task, September 2026): the 116 source
    packages that ended APPLY_FAILED or UPLOAD_GIVEUP are excluded
    from the default LTO build on all architectures (any), so that
    the arm64 / sw64 / loong64 rebuilds do not trip over them.
    20 of them are also on Ubuntu's list; the rest are UOS-specific
    findings.
  * Reference baseline: Ubuntu lto-disabled-list v81, minus the
    qt6-* entries: deepin builds the Qt6 stack with LTO by default
    (explicit optimize=+lto in deepin-community qt6-* debian/rules),
    keep them enabled.

